{"_id":"68f89af0166b018f83dfb0c1","roadmapSlug":"swift-ui","nodeId":"4EBdMshXiAylkgoG9FqlB","description":"# Operators in Swift\n\nOperators are special symbols or phrases that you use to check, change, or combine values. Swift supports a variety of operators, from familiar arithmetic operators like `+` and `-`, to more advanced operators for logic and bit manipulation. These operators allow you to perform calculations, make comparisons, and manipulate data within your Swift code.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Basic operators","url":"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/documentation/the-swift-programming-language/basicoperators/","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1648e"},{"type":"official","title":"Advanced Operators","url":"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/documentation/the-swift-programming-language/advancedoperators/","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1648f"},{"type":"article","title":"Swift Operators","url":"https://www.programiz.com/swift-programming/operators","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16490"},{"type":"article","title":"The Ultimate Guide to Operators in Swift","url":"https://www.appypievibe.ai/blog/swift-code/operators-swift-how-to/","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16491"},{"type":"video","title":"Introduction to Swift: Operators","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Svaq3jVy8sU","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16492"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-22T08:50:56.829Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:22:09.974Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/swift-ui/content/4EBdMshXiAylkgoG9FqlB.md"}